Zeo patch 0005 — send the assistant message id to LiteLLM beside the chat id.

Target: Open WebUI v0.12.3 (ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.12.3).
Applied by ai/openwebui/Dockerfile.openwebui with `patch -p1` from /app.

Upstream: with ENABLE_FORWARD_USER_INFO_HEADERS=true, every request to an
OpenAI-compatible connection carries X-OpenWebUI-User-Name/-Id/-Email/-Role,
and a chat-completions request also carries X-OpenWebUI-Chat-Id
(utils/headers.py, get_headers_and_cookies — in routers/openai.py until
v0.12.0, now shared with the Ollama router). X-OpenWebUI-Message-Id
(FORWARD_SESSION_INFO_HEADER_MESSAGE_ID, already defined in env.py) is only
sent to tool servers (utils/tools.py, build_tool_server_headers), so LiteLLM
can tell which chat a request belongs to but not which turn.

This patch adds the message id in the same place and under the same guards
as the chat id: the flag is on, there is a user, and the request's metadata
has a `message_id`. Only the chat paths pass metadata
(routers/openai.py::generate_chat_completion, and routers/ollama.py's
send_request for its chat / completion calls), so the header goes on
chat-completions requests only. On a chat sent from the UI
the value is the id of the ASSISTANT message being generated
(main.py::chat_completion, per_model_metadata['message_id']): one per model
in a multi-model chat, a new one on regenerate, and the same one on every
tool-round follow-up and auto-continue nudge of that turn. Task-model calls
(title, tags, follow-ups, queries) carry the chat id but no message id. A
direct API caller gets the `id` it sent, if any.

Used by the LiteLLM route-policy hook (ai/litellm/hooks/routing/) to key
shadow decisions to a chat turn. No new env var: ENABLE_FORWARD_USER_INFO_HEADERS
(compose: ${OPENWEBUI_ENABLE_FORWARD_USER_INFO_HEADERS:-false}) turns both
ids on or off; FORWARD_SESSION_INFO_HEADER_MESSAGE_ID renames the header.

Files: backend/open_webui/utils/headers.py.
See ai/openwebui/OPENWEBUI.md § Forwarded user and session headers and
§ Custom image. Tests: unit-tests/openwebui/ (run the patched block straight
out of this file).

